{"author":"John Wesley","book":"Notes on the Bible","chapter":803,"classification":{"bucket":"Christian Classics / Commentaries","canonicalStatus":"noncanonical","contentKind":"commentary","cautionReason":"","doctrinalStatus":"historical","labels":["christian-classics","commentaries"],"severity":0},"id":"classics:wesley:Ps.66","lineage":[],"metadata":{"author":"John Wesley","authorshipDateRange":"18th century","genre":"Commentaries","tradition":"Methodist","translator":null,"edition":"CCEL edition; source omits 2 Samuel 24","rights":"Public Domain","source":{"id":"wesley","provider":"CCEL","sourceUrl":"https://www.ccel.org/ccel/wesley/notes.html","title":"Notes on the Bible"}},"originalBook":"Psalms","sourceVolumeId":"wesley","source":{"id":"wesley","sourceUrl":"https://www.ccel.org/ccel/wesley/notes.html","title":"Notes on the Bible"},"title":"Psalms 66","reference":"Psalms 66","notes":[],"verses":[{"verse":1,"text":"The psalmist calls on all people to praise God, for his sovereign power over the whole creation, ver.","sourceParagraph":1},{"verse":2,"text":"1-7.","sourceParagraph":1},{"verse":3,"text":"For his special favour to his people, ver.","sourceParagraph":1},{"verse":4,"text":"8-12.","sourceParagraph":1},{"verse":5,"text":"Praises him for his goodness to himself in particular, ver.","sourceParagraph":1},{"verse":6,"text":"13-20.","sourceParagraph":1},{"verse":7,"text":"To the chief musician, A song or psalm.","sourceParagraph":1},{"verse":8,"text":"1.","sourceParagraph":2,"scriptureVerseStart":1,"scriptureVerseEnd":1},{"verse":9,"text":"All lands - Ye people of all nations.","sourceParagraph":2,"scriptureVerseStart":1,"scriptureVerseEnd":1},{"verse":10,"text":"He invites the Gentile world, to the contemplation and celebration of God's works.","sourceParagraph":2,"scriptureVerseStart":1,"scriptureVerseEnd":1},{"verse":11,"text":"6.","sourceParagraph":3,"scriptureVerseStart":6,"scriptureVerseEnd":6},{"verse":12,"text":"We - Our nation, or our ancestors, in whose loins we then were.","sourceParagraph":3,"scriptureVerseStart":6,"scriptureVerseEnd":6},{"verse":13,"text":"10.","sourceParagraph":4,"scriptureVerseStart":10,"scriptureVerseEnd":10},{"verse":14,"text":"Proved us - As it were in a burning furnace; and with a design to purge out our dross.","sourceParagraph":4,"scriptureVerseStart":10,"scriptureVerseEnd":10},{"verse":15,"text":"11.","sourceParagraph":5,"scriptureVerseStart":11,"scriptureVerseEnd":11},{"verse":16,"text":"Net - Which our enemies laid for us.","sourceParagraph":5,"scriptureVerseStart":11,"scriptureVerseEnd":11},{"verse":17,"text":"12.","sourceParagraph":6,"scriptureVerseStart":12,"scriptureVerseEnd":12},{"verse":18,"text":"To ride - To use us like slaves.","sourceParagraph":6,"scriptureVerseStart":12,"scriptureVerseEnd":12},{"verse":19,"text":"15.","sourceParagraph":7,"scriptureVerseStart":15,"scriptureVerseEnd":15},{"verse":20,"text":"I will go - One speaks in the name of all the rest.","sourceParagraph":7,"scriptureVerseStart":15,"scriptureVerseEnd":15},{"verse":21,"text":"Incense - With the fat of rams, which is no less pleasing to God than incense.","sourceParagraph":7,"scriptureVerseStart":15,"scriptureVerseEnd":15},{"verse":22,"text":"18.","sourceParagraph":8,"scriptureVerseStart":18,"scriptureVerseEnd":18},{"verse":23,"text":"Iniquity - Any sin.","sourceParagraph":8,"scriptureVerseStart":18,"scriptureVerseEnd":18},{"verse":24,"text":"In heart - If my heart had been false to God, although I might have forborne outward acts.","sourceParagraph":8,"scriptureVerseStart":18,"scriptureVerseEnd":18},{"verse":25,"text":"If I had been guilty of that, by heart was set upon sin, or I desired only that which I resolved in my heart to spend upon my lusts.","sourceParagraph":8,"scriptureVerseStart":18,"scriptureVerseEnd":18}],"scriptureReference":{"book":"Psalms","chapter":66}}